            <ArticleTitle>Intra-articular bupivacaine for pain relief after arthroscopic surgery of the knee joint in daycase patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>563-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A randomised double-blind study was conducted to compare the influence on postoperative pain of equal volumes of one of two concentrations of bupivacaine (0.25%, 0.5%), or saline 0.9%, injected into the knee joint after arthroscopy. The results showed that intra-articular bupivacaine had no significant analgesic effect in either concentration. Plasma bupivacaine concentrations were measured 20 minutes after injection in order to determine the extent of systemic absorption.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
